 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? There are few that have been read aloud in classrooms, like So You Want Go Back to Kindy or The 39 Clues. Or check the kid's section at your local library. Then look up podcast episodes that feature the author reading one of her books. It' a great way to get her interested in reading. As long as you listen together and stop if she feels uncomfortable, they're great for building an audio library. Not yet. Lots of early podcasts were made at bedtime, and some kids doze off. Keep the room bright and be there when she gets off.",
